<title>UK: Philippines become 48th member of ISO.</title>
<headline>Philippines become 48th member of ISO.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippines has become party to the 1992 International Sugar Agreement, making it the 48th member of the International Sugar Organization (ISO), the ISO said in a statement on Thursday.</p>
<p>It became party to the Agreement on October 23, the ISO added.</p>
<p>IN 1995, the Philippines produced 1.56 million tonnes of sugar raw value, exported 155,000 tonnes, imported 377,000 tonnes and consumed 1.77 million tonnes.</p>
<p>With the addition of the Philippines, the ISO's member countries represented 67 percent of world sugar production and 48 percent of consumption, based on data for 1995, the ISO said. They accounted for 88 percent of world sugar exports and 20 percent of imports, it added.</p>
<p>Costa Rica became the ISO's 47th member on October 11.</p>
<p>-- Jeremy Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
